# Hash-pinned test fixtures must be byte-identical on EVERY platform.
#
# Why this file exists: tests/test_r94_golden.py pins the golden fixture by sha256 of its raw
# bytes. With core.autocrlf=true (the default on the Windows dev machine) git stores LF in the
# blob but checks out CRLF in the working tree, while Linux CI checks out LF — so the same
# committed file hashed to two different digests and the golden went red on CI only. Marking the
# fixture `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion, so the working tree bytes equal the blob
# bytes everywhere.
#
# The test additionally hashes newline-NORMALISED content, so a stale clone that predates this
# file still passes. Belt and braces: neither layer weakens the gate — a real content change
# still changes the digest.
tests/fixtures/r94_golden_ohlcv.csv -text
tests/fixtures/r94_golden_expected.json -text
